WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.420
It's a new day on Tesla Short's time, daily episode 498, coming to you from Vancouver,

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:14.180
it's June 3, 2026. Plenty going on in EV land, let's get to it. Halifax gets its first

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:19.580
supercharger site under construction, extending the network into Atlantic Canada for the first time.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:26.200
US EV registrations fell for the eighth straight month according to fresh motor intelligence data.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.060
The decline spans multiple models and occurs against rising competition

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:37.080
plus shifting buyer incentives. Tesla has not announced major pricing or inventory moves to

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:43.180
address the pattern. The streak raises questions about demand elasticity in the largest EV market.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.840
Earnings commentary later this quarter may address any mitigation steps.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.340
While sales pressure builds at home, Tesla is still pushing software forward with the latest

00:00:53.340 --> 00:01:03.600
FSD updates. Revised Tesla FSD V14.3.3 is now installing on model Y vehicles equipped with the

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.860
latest hardware. Owners report the updated package following the broader V14 series that brought

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:16.640
incremental perception and control improvements. The revision targets specific edge cases identified

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.980
during earlier supervised testing. The rollout continues as Tesla refines the stack ahead of

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:29.780
wider unsupervised ambitions. Next, watch for release notes or owner reports on behavior changes

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:37.900
in complex urban scenarios. Tesla informed Australian owners that FSD supervised V14 for hardware

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:44.440
four vehicles remains in final local development and testing. The message indicates region-specific

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:51.140
validation is nearing completion before wider deployment. HW4 cars in Australia have waited

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:57.440
longer than some other markets for the latest supervised version. This step addresses local regulatory

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:03.840
and mapping requirements that differ from North American conditions. Attendant listeners should monitor

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:10.120
for the first confirmed installs in the coming weeks. As the software keeps evolving, Tesla is also

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:15.800
using social channels to keep the conversation light. The official Tesla account posted an image

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:23.560
captioned. My car also has FSD alongside a humorous vehicle comparison. The post continues the

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:29.400
pattern of using light social content to highlight the features growing presence during the V14 rollout.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.700
Tesla also posted a playful reference to the fictional smuggler's bay with the line.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:40.540
The first rule of smuggler's bay is, you do not talk about smuggler's bay, geez.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:47.160
The account often uses short humorous posts to engage followers outside technical updates.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:54.340
It shows the brand maintaining a casual tone on X even as major programs advance. Tesla reached

00:02:54.340 --> 00:03:00.120
a new cumulative sales threshold in the United Kingdom amid rising pressure from European and Chinese

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:06.980
rivals. The milestone reflects steady demand for the Model Y and Model 3 despite a broader market

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:12.840
slowdown. Local pricing adjustments and availability of refreshed variants supported the result.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.980
The company now faces direct competition from several new battery electric entrants in the same

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:24.600
segments. Future quarters will show whether the UK trajectory holds against these challenges.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:30.580
The Model X ranked as the top-selling used electric vehicle in recent North American data,

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:37.100
while hybrid models continued gaining share overall. Strong residual values for the 3-row

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:42.240
SEV reflect sustained demand from buyers seeking larger battery electric options.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:47.680
The result stands out against slower used EV volume growth in other segments.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:53.100
Tesla's earlier production ramp and warranty coverage likely contribute to the model's

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:58.340
appeal on the secondary market. Observers will track whether refreshed Model X inventory

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:05.280
sustains this position. BYD leads EV sales in the UK, Australia and Brazil combined.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:12.620
BYD now leads EV sales in the UK, Australia and Brazil combined after aggressive pricing

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:18.500
and faster model refreshes. Tesla's overseas volumes grew but not enough to hold the top

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:24.300
position in those regions. The change highlights how quickly market leadership can move when multiple

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.800
competitors scale simultaneously. The same competitive pressure is visible in emerging markets,

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:37.480
where BYD has already taken a large share of Africa. BYD secured roughly one-third of electric

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:42.300
vehicle sales across African markets through aggressive pricing and local partnerships.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:49.480
Tesla's later entry focuses on establishing a foothold via a planned presence in Morocco rather

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:54.860
than immediate volume across the continent. The contrast highlights differing go-to-market

00:04:54.860 --> 00:05:00.600
approaches between the two companies in emerging regions. Infrastructure limitations and price

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:06.900
sensitivity remain key barriers for any brand. The Morocco strategy will be watched for its ability

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:13.900
to generate meaningful volume. Electric vehicles nudge 30% sales share as Tesla Model Y becomes

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:20.400
Australia's best-selling car. Battery electric vehicles reached nearly 30% of new car sales in

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:26.880
Australia during May, with the Model Y claiming the overall top spot. The result marks the first

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:33.260
time EVs crossed that threshold in a single month. Multiple Chinese brands also posted strong numbers,

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:39.900
widening buyer choice in the segment. The Model Y's position reflects both competitive pricing

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:46.020
and established charging infrastructure. Continued growth will depend on supply of refreshed

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:53.780
variants and home charger adoption. Model YL long wheelbase variant spotted at Fremont. A longer

00:05:53.780 --> 00:06:00.000
wheelbase Model Y variant appeared during testing at the Fremont facility. The sightings suggest

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.940
continued development of an extended range or seven-seat configuration. No official confirmation

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:11.600
or specifications have been released by Tesla. The vehicle's presence at the California plant

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:17.860
indicates the program remains active alongside other refresh efforts. Production timing and market

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:23.540
allocation remain open questions. That platform flexibility ties directly into how Tesla

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:28.720
approaches engineering decisions overall. Taking a step back from today's headlines,

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:34.220
the appearance of a longer wheelbase Model Y at the Fremont test track challenges the assumption

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:39.200
that Tesla only iterates on existing platforms rather than spawning distinct variants.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:44.720
The sighting suggests the company is willing to stretch the Model Y architecture for specific

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:51.040
market or seating needs without waiting for an all-new skateboard. This approach keeps development

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:56.860
costs and timelines shorter than starting from a clean sheet. Engineering data from prior Tesla

00:06:56.860 --> 00:07:04.000
refreshes shows that wheelbase extensions of roughly 150 to 200 millimeters can be achieved with

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:10.480
relatively modest changes to structural castings and battery pack length. Those changes preserve

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:16.160
the majority of shared tooling and supplier relationships while unlocking new cargo or passenger

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:22.760
configurations. The economics favor this route when the incremental volume justifies the added complexity

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:28.500
at the assembly plant. The practical implication is that Tesla can respond to segment gaps

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:34.960
such as seven-seat demand or longer range utility without diverting resources from next-generation

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:41.840
programs. If the Model YL reaches production, it would test whether buyers value the added space

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:48.020
enough to offset any efficiency or handling trade-offs. The next visible signal will be whether

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:54.400
similar variants appear in regulatory filings or at other test locations. While the product-side

00:07:54.400 --> 00:08:00.920
experiments with variants, the charging network is quietly expanding in new regions. Construction began

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:07.440
on the initial supercharger location in Halifax, Nova Scotia. The sight represents the first permanent

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:13.560
DC fast-charging installation in the province for Tesla vehicles. Local owners have previously

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:19.980
relied on destination chargers or longer drives to reach the nearest stations. The project aligns

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:26.200
with Tesla's gradual expansion of the network into secondary Canadian markets. Completion timing

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:32.600
and stall count will determine usability for regional travel. Network growth abroad contrasts

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:38.600
with an unexpected fleet win closer to home. Emergency services in Kazakhstan placed an order for

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:45.240
cyber truck units marking an unexpected government fleet adoption. The vehicles will serve operational

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:51.640
roles where durability and off-road capability matter. Tesla has not disclosed pricing or delivery

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:57.760
schedules for the export market. The sale demonstrates interest beyond the initial North American customer

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:04.080
base. Future fleet orders could provide additional volume signals for the model. That fleet interest

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:09.520
sits alongside Tesla's broader push into used car strength and regional sales milestones.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:15.880
Rivian R2 performance claims edge over model-wide performance in a recent car buzz comparison.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:22.160
The analysis sites advantages in ride quality, interior space, and certain performance metrics.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:29.120
Rivian has not yet begun customer deliveries of the R2, so real-world data remains limited.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:34.620
The comparison underscores growing competition in the performance SUV segment.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:40.260
A fleet operator shared video of a Tesla semi climbing California's grapevine grade

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:45.560
with a full trailer. The operator described the performance as impressive given the payload.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:50.980
The demonstration adds to limited public data on real-world semi-capability.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:56.100
Production volume and additional fleet orders remain the next milestones to watch.

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:02.740
Tesla filed a legal action in Manitoba to recover rebates previously denied on certain vehicle

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:09.200
sales. The case centers on eligibility rules that the company argues were applied inconsistently.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:15.540
A favorable ruling could affect similar programs and other provinces. The outcome will clarify

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:21.640
how rebate frameworks treat direct sales models. Nearly all major EV makers plan to drop

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:29.480
native CCS-1 ports by the 2027 model year in favor of NACS. Only a handful of holdouts remain,

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:35.640
mostly lower volume name plates. The transition simplifies charging access for Tesla owners and

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:42.280
non-Tesla drivers using the network. Remaining CCS-1 vehicles will require adapters for broader

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:48.440
compatibility. There is a challenge worth discussing. US registrations fell for the eighth straight

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:54.500
month spanning multiple models amid rising competition. The street coincides with broader market

00:10:54.500 --> 00:11:01.280
shifts toward hybrids and new EV entrants. Tesla has not detailed specific inventory or pricing

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:07.460
responses in the latest data release. The trend raises the question of whether recent software and

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:13.520
hardware updates can reverse buyer hesitation before the next earnings report. Tomorrow we'll be

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:21.340
watching for any first confirmed FSDV14 installs in Australia and further details on the Model YL

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:33.540
testing program. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $423.74 up $7.86 1.9%.

